<header><p class="st-kicker">county · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Lordships of Schönburg</h1><p class="st-meta">1170 CE – 1740 CE (approx.) · capital Glauchau</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Cluster of lordships in western Saxony held by the Schönburg family for six centuries, balanced uneasily between imperial immediacy and Saxon control.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-schonburg">Schönburgs</a> were imperial ministerials from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saale">Saale</a> region near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naumburg">Naumburg</a>. From about 1170 they were granted lands in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pleissenland">Pleissenland</a>, the imperial territory around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/altenburg">Altenburg</a>, and built up lordships along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zwickauer-mulde">Zwickauer Mulde</a> centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glauchau">Glauchau</a>, later adding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waldenburg-saxony">Waldenburg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lichtenstein-saxony">Lichtenstein</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hartenstein-saxony">Hartenstein</a>. These were held directly from the Empire, which gave the family the standing of minor imperial lords.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The lordships were ruled by several branches of the family from castles in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glauchau">Glauchau</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waldenburg-saxony">Waldenburg</a>, with small towns, farmland and later textile crafts in the valley. The family adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lutheranism">Lutheranism</a> in the 16th century. Their position was squeezed by the neighbouring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-wettin">Wettin</a> rulers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>, who held some Schönburg lands as fiefs and steadily claimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> over the rest.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>By the recesses agreed with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/electorate-of-saxony">Electorate of Saxony</a>, culminating in 1740, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-schonburg">Schönburgs</a> accepted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> while keeping special rights of administration and justice. These lingered into the 19th century, and the family remained major landowners in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> until 1945.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="county, 1170 CE – 1740 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">county</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:82.99%;width:11.34%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1170 CE – 1740 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Glauchau</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism, then Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Schönburg, Schönburg-Glauchau</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1455&amp;focus=lordships-of-schonburg" aria-label="Lordships of Schönburg on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4965 414 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lordships of Schönburg lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5285 670L5229 694M52